# Free Skolem constants for the law checks: no axiom mentions them, so
# a law verified on them holds for arbitrary values (fresh-constant
# argument). Both sides of every equivalence query reference THE SAME
# module existential, which is what makes the two independently loaded
# query modules talk about one entity.

∃ e1; ∃ e2; ∃ e3;
∃ x0; ∃ y0; ∃ g0;
∃ v0; ∃ m0; ∃ op0;
